      "statement": "mcp-shared is a library (not a Worker) holding exactly the code where two divergent copies would become a security bug — tool classification, scope grammar, OAuth lifecycle, approval-queue wiring — while each MCP connector keeps its own vendor entrypoint, DOs, connect form, and configurator and varies shared behavior only through named hooks.",
